      "Ionic / Electrovalent Bonding: Electrostatic attraction between oppositely charged ions formed by electron transfer; favored by low ionization energy of metal, high electron affinity of non-metal, and high Lattice Energy.",
      "Lattice Energy & Born-Haber Cycle: Lattice energy U is energy released when 1 mole of solid ionic crystal forms from gaseous ions: M^+(g) + X^-(g) \\to MX(s); calculated via Born-Haber thermochemical cycle: \\Delta H_f^\\circ = \\Delta H_{sub} + \\frac{1}{2}\\Delta H_{diss} + \\text{IE} + \\text{EA} + U.",
      "Fajan's Rules for Covalent Character in Ionic Bonds: Covalent character increases with: (1) Small cation size, (2) Large anion size, (3) High ionic charge on cation or anion, (4) Cation with pseudo-noble gas configuration (18 valence electrons, e.g. Cu^+, Ag^+).",
      "Valence Bond Theory (VBT) & Orbital Overlap: Covalent bond forms by pairing of electrons in overlapping half-filled atomic orbitals; \\sigma-bond formed by axial / head-on overlap (stronger); \\pi-bond formed by lateral / sideways overlap (weaker).",
      "Orbital Hybridization: Mixing of non-equivalent atomic orbitals to form equivalent hybrid orbitals: sp (linear 180°, BeCl_2, ethyne), sp^2 (trigonal planar 120°, BF_3, ethene), sp^3 (tetrahedral 109.5°, CH_4), sp^3d (trigonal bipyramidal, PCl_5), sp^3d^2 (octahedral 90°, SF_6).",
      "VSEPR Theory (Valence Shell Electron Pair Repulsion): Molecular geometry determined solely by repulsions between valence electron pairs: Repulsion magnitude: \\text{lone pair-lone pair (lp-lp)} > \\text{lone pair-bond pair (lp-bp)} > \\text{bond pair-bond pair (bp-bp)}; explains bent geometry of H_2O (104.5°) and pyramidal NH_3 (107°).",
      "Molecular Orbital Theory (MOT): Atomic orbitals combine via LCAO into bonding (\\sigma, \\pi) and antibonding (\\sigma^*, \\pi^*) MOs; Bond Order = \\frac{N_b - N_a}{2}; correctly predicts paramagnetism of O_2 (two unpaired electrons in \\pi^*_{2p}).",
