      "Bromination Selectivity: Highly selective for tertiary C-H bonds (ratio 1600:82:1).",
      "Markovnikov Addition Rule: Proton H+ adds to double-bond carbon with more hydrogens.",
      "Peroxide Effect Specificity: Operates strictly with HBr (fails with HCl and HI).",
      "Ozonolysis Diagnostic Utility: Cleaves double bond into carbonyls to locate double bond position.",
      "Baeyer's Unsaturation Test: Cold alkaline KMnO_4 decolors from purple to brown MnO_2 precipitate.",
      "Terminal Alkyne Acidity: Terminal alkynes react with NaNH_2 or ammoniacal AgNO_3 forming metal acetylides.",
      "Lindlar Catalyst Yield: Selectively hydrogenates alkynes to Cis-alkenes.",
      "Birch Reduction Yield: Selectively reduces alkynes to Trans-alkenes.",
      "Diels-Alder Reaction: [4+2] concerted cycloaddition between diene and dienophile.",
